        "file_text": "# ClearDent ETG Project - Dale Carnegie Sales Training\n\n**Deal ID:** 59369911869\n**Status:** Not yet submitted\n**Training Dates:** June 9 - July 28, 2026\n**Approved Funding:** $2,516.48\n\n## Company: Prococious Technology Inc. (DBA ClearDent)\n- **Industry:** Healthcare technology / dental SaaS\n- **Founded:** 2002 in British Columbia\n- **Market:** Serves 35,000+ dental professionals across Canada\n- **Product:** All-in-one dental practice management software (scheduling, billing, charting, imaging, patient comms, analytics)\n- **Market Context:** Competitive dental software market shifting toward cloud adoption, automation, patient engagement, data-driven practice management\n\n## Training\n- **Course:** Dale Carnegie Sales Training: Winning with Relationship Selling\n- **Provider:** Dale Carnegie\n- **Duration:** 8 weeks, 28 hours (1 night/week)\n- **Cost:** $2,516.48\n- **Format:** Discussion, practical exercises, presentations, classroom exercises\n- **Learning Outcomes:** Relationship-based sales strategies, customer connection techniques, collaborative solution building, objection handling, repeat business maintenance\n\n## Participant\n- **Name:** Nitin Lall\n- **Email:** nlall@cleardent.com\n- **Position:** Account Manager\n- **Tenure:** 1 year 9 months at ClearDent\n- **Background:** Exceptional account management skills, previous work also focused on account management\n- **Skills Gap:** NO formal sales training (this is a new skill for him)\n- **Recent Changes:** Received pay raise + increase in targets/KPIs\n- **Compensation:** Commission-based role\n- **Better Job Outcome:** Increased earnings through improved commission performance (better sales conversion/upsell skills)\n\n## Business Justification\n**Complex B2B SaaS sales environment:**\n- High-stakes purchases for dental clinics (significant financial commitment, migration risk)\n- Long decision cycles with multiple stakeholders\n- Requires consultative selling, objection handling, value articulation\n\n**Competitive market:**\n- Competitors: Dentrix, Curve, Tracker\n- Need to differentiate beyond features → value-based selling\n- Price sensitivity and switching concerns\n\n**Industry shift:**\n- Cloud migration conversations\n- Change management (resistance from established clinics)\n- Data security/compliance concerns (PHIPA)\n- Need to guide prospects through transformation, not just demo software\n\n**Growth goals:**\n- Expand into multi-location practices and DSOs\n- Upsell additional modules (patient engagement, cloud migration, analytics)\n- Improve retention and reduce churn\n- Requires strong relationship-building and strategic account management\n\n## Eligibility Status\n✅ Training type: Structured 8-week course (NOT seminar)\n✅ Duration: 28 hours over 8 weeks\n✅ Cost: $2,516.48 (under $10,000)\n✅ Learning outcomes: Specific, skills-based\n✅ Participant: BC resident, employed, no formal sales training\n✅ Better job outcome: Clear (increased commission earnings)\n\n## Workflow Status\n- [x] Eligibility verified\n- [x] Company/participant info gathered\n- [ ] Questions 1-3 drafted\n- [ ] BC alternatives researched\n- [ ] Questions 4-7 drafted\n"
